rs, lube filters, air filters, crankcase ventilation, hydraulic filters and coolants and other chemicals for on-highway commercial vehicles and off-highway agriculture, construction, mining, and power generation vehicles and equipment. The company also develops filtration technologies, including filtration media, filter element formation, filtration systems integration; and service-related solutions, such as remote digital diagnostic and prognostic platforms, and analytics. Atmus Filtration Technologies Inc. was founded in 1958 and is headquartered in Nashville, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Stephanie Juanita Disher | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $392K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $33K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Atmus Filtration Technologies I is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $4.2B market cap on $1.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 37% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 27-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 28%.","The business throws off $149M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.98\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.9%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Carries a 37% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.36618237430701583},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 22% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Will Atmus Filtration (NYSE:ATMU) Benefit From Rising Dividend?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/will-atmus-filtration-nyseatmu-benefit-from-rising-dividend","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795195500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.459,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Atmus Filtration Technologies (NYSE:ATMU) versus RBC Bearings (NYSE:RBC) Head to Head Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/atmus-filtration-technologies-nyseatmu-versus-rbc-bearings-nyserbc-head-to-head-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794823217.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Tesla Revive China Sales While Ramping Up Shanghai Output?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032955/can-tesla-revive-china-sales-while-ramping-up-shanghai-output?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Ccompany_news_corporate_actions-3032955","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795180500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Laura Heltebran Awarded 5,070 RSUs at Atmus Filtration for Interim Chief People Officer Duties","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/laura-heltebran-awarded-5070-rsus-at-atmus-filtration-for-interim-chief-people-officer-duties","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795175220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Atmus Filtration Grants Laura Heltebran $30K Monthly Stipend and $250K Equity as Interim CPO","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/anno